 {"kind":"lesson","scope":"p3/runtime/showroom-1773-unattended-editor-lifetime","tags":["incident","regression","assistant-recorded","verbatim-source"],"title":"P3 showroom cold start still consumes nearly the full bounded proof session","text":"On 2026-09-06, P3 #1773 reproduced a long cold-start incident even after the hard-paging classifier was corrected. Worker-owned UnrealEditor-Cmd PID 23128 launched offscreen at 02:04:22Z and did not report editorReady=true until about 02:14:22Z (~600 seconds). During startup, physical RAM was very low but commit headroom remained large and Test-P3BuildHardPaging correctly stayed false, so this was not the old false hard-paging stop. PIE then started and a canonical same-world player-camera PNG was captured successfully at 02:15:29Z. Before a follow-up authored CAM_Overview capture could run, the launcher-enforced 900-second lifetime expired and PID 23128 disappeared; a foreign #1634 Unreal editor was then the only live Unreal process, preventing immediate relaunch. Recurrence lesson: the 900-second bounded lifetime is still practically too short for a ~600-second cold showroom start plus proof/review work. Preserve the lifetime bound, but the owner should distinguish startup budget from post-ready proof budget or otherwise guarantee bounded usable time after readiness. This incident is unresolved and should be treated as recurring history, not current runtime authority.","state":"PROVEN","evidence":["github:organicoverlords/p3#1773","C:\\P3Proofs\\showroom1773-baseline-20260906-021523\\baseline.png sha256=e4d06efccf6b4a9474363725bbf207a90dd9d216d1f07d57d9a822c1b5b2027d","Invoke-P3UnattendedEditor start=2026-09-06T02:04:22.885Z ready=2026-09-06T02:14:27.361Z startup_timeout=600 lifetime_timeout=900 pid=23128","health_check editorReady=true at 2026-09-06T02:14:22Z; PIE status isPlaying=true; canonical capture completed 2026-09-06T02:15:29Z"],"supersedes":[],"source_messages":["so save this incident in vault so you know it happens still"],"interpretation":"The user explicitly asked that this recurrence be durable. The stable finding is that the corrected memory-pressure guard no longer falsely kills startup, but a separate bounded-lifetime design still allows a successful ~10-minute cold start to consume most of a 15-minute runtime lease and expire during proof collection. The record should help future debugging avoid misattributing the recurrence to hard paging or LFS hydration.","confidence":98,"confidence_reason":"Direct live process timestamps, bridge health, successful PIE/capture output, subsequent PID disappearance at the 900-second bound, and foreign-editor-only process evidence were observed in this execution turn.","project":"p3","thread":"thread:p3-showroom-unattended-runtime","turn_task":"go","id":"mem-20260906-1a206c05","timestamp":"2026-09-06T05:28:07+03:00"}
 {"kind":"lesson","scope":"vault/timeline/materialized-ingestion","tags":["timeline","materialization","incremental-ingestion","work-graph","performance","assistant-recorded","verbatim-source"],"title":"Vault timeline aggregates once and readers consume materialized deltas","text":"Vault timeline aggregation is owned by one periodic materializer, not by bootstrap or each worker. A one-time 30-day backfill builds the local corpus; subsequent refreshes use per-source last-success watermarks with a 10-minute overlap and stable event-id deduplication, retaining unchanged history locally. Bootstrap reads only the compact projection. Live proof after #616: 12,213-event backfill in 149.3s; next incremental refresh read 105 delta observations in 24.8s; first scheduled refresh read 103 delta observations in 18.6s with no saturated source; bootstrap read the fresh materialization in 287.8ms internal / 496ms wall. The work graph joined equivalent branch/main commits by stable patch-id and attached PR, Action, worker duration/utilization, memory/proof evidence where anchored.","state":"PROVEN","evidence":["github:organicoverlords/regression-research#616","git:organicoverlords/regression-research@8883e10b8b22e4361f40c5f884bc553cdd7472cd","task:Vault Timeline Materializer","worker-report:manual-20260906T0452-vault-timeline-ingestion-graph"],"supersedes":[],"source_messages":["study more and improve the timeline so its not costly and ingests automatically data and expand the graph thing if you see fit","make timeline part of vault that just runs periodically and bootstrap polls a small part of it","without each bootstrap having to do that each time for each worker, timeline handles it once whenever","why would you refresh thousands of items its not like the history changes?"],"interpretation":"The durable invariant is cheap readers plus incremental periodic ingestion: immutable history stays in the local materialized corpus and normal refreshes collect only deltas. Full horizon scans are explicit backfills, not recurring work. Work-equivalence and continuity-case graphs remain separate derived history views, never current runtime authority.","confidence":100,"confidence_reason":"PR #616 required verification passed; the merged live script completed an explicit backfill, a manual incremental refresh, a real scheduled incremental refresh with Last Result 0, and a sub-second materialized bootstrap read.","thread":"vault-timeline-materialized-ingestion","turn_task":"study more and improve the timeline so its not costly and ingests automatically data and expand the graph thing if you see fit","id":"mem-20260906-ded71f72","timestamp":"2026-09-06T06:16:28+03:00"}
 {"kind":"lesson","scope":"vault/timeline/materialized-ingestion","tags":["timeline","debugging","coverage","materialization","assistant-recorded","verbatim-source"],"title":"Timeline debugging preserves uncertainty across fresh deltas","text":"Bootstrap, Vault overview, and targeted timeline queries must share one materialized freshness/coverage contract while remaining below live owner evidence for current diagnosis. Historical backfill saturation must persist across later clean incremental refreshes; stale materialization or a pending source retry also makes a timeline miss non-authoritative. In those states a no-match result is not proof of absence. Targeted work-graph output must be query-scoped and bounded so shared worker reports do not fan topical queries into unrelated work. Materializer lock overlap is a successful no-op for periodic scheduling, not a task failure.","state":"PROVEN","evidence":["github:organicoverlords/regression-research#623","github:organicoverlords/regression-research#624","git:organicoverlords/regression-research@f57242fde1db446806fa4c1151f702401ce1f6cb","git:organicoverlords/regression-research@cf9876771d7b93e004c70a4e7171f694ef4a346e","task:Vault Timeline Materializer","worker-report:manual-20260906T0626-vault-bootstrap-timeline-coherence"],"supersedes":[],"source_messages":["make sure bootstrap and timeline and vault are coherent user experience now and does not generate debugging or inconsistency problems like making your hierarchy have holes or make you stupid in debugging etc like before"],"interpretation":"The verified hierarchy is: current live repo/runtime/scheduler/coordinator evidence owns current truth; the materialized Vault timeline supplies bounded historical orientation and lineage. Freshness, source coverage, and absence semantics must be identical across bootstrap/overview/timeline, and historical uncertainty cannot be erased by a healthy recent delta.","confidence":100,"confidence_reason":"PR #623 required verification passed and live rebuild re-measured github/repos/runner_logs historical saturation; the next clean incremental retained those debt fields. Live bootstrap, overview, and a no-match query all returned the same HISTORICAL_INCOMPLETE / NO_MATCH_IS_NOT_PROOF_OF_ABSENCE semantics. PR #624 required verification passed and a fresh-lock CLI proof returned exit 0.","thread":"vault-timeline-materialized-ingestion","turn_task":"make sure bootstrap and timeline and vault are coherent user experience now and does not generate debugging or inconsistency problems like making your hierarchy have holes or make you stupid in debugging etc like before","id":"mem-20260906-bc795b46","timestamp":"2026-09-06T06:48:27+03:00"}
+{"kind":"fact","scope":"Tiny3D issue #9","tags":["performance","proof","assistant-recorded","verbatim-source"],"title":"Tiny3D exact library show and P3 attribution gap","text":"Tiny3D PR #348 merged at 319de296: exact-directory library show bypasses full-library indexing, and import PASS receipts missing execution identity surface p3_execution_attribution. Fresh asset 245a1e11 is hash-bound/valid but omits p3_commit and build_identity, so it remains P3_HANDOFF_VERIFIED. Real lookup measured 6.849s after the patch versus ~128s before.","state":"PROVEN","evidence":["https://github.com/organicoverlords/tiny3d/pull/348 ; https://github.com/organicoverlords/tiny3d/issues/9#issuecomment-5556851697"],"supersedes":[],"source_messages":["work on tiny3d"],"interpretation":"Reusable troubleshooting fact for Tiny3D/P3 proof work. It records a merged Tiny3D behavior and the exact currently observed producer-side metadata gap; future work must reverify live state before treating the P3 gap as current.","confidence":99,"confidence_reason":"Direct live receipt inspection, real CLI replay, 826 local CI-equivalent tests, hosted PR-head CI success, and merged PR #348.","project":"tiny3d","turn_task":"work on tiny3d","id":"mem-20260906-8a553cf1","timestamp":"2026-09-06T07:19:49+03:00"}
+{"kind":"lesson","scope":"vault/timeline/materialized-ingestion","tags":["timeline","debugging","narrative","bootstrap","assistant-recorded","verbatim-source"],"title":"Timeline answers lead with cases, not evidence volume or umbrella anchors","text":"Timeline consumers must narrate continuity cases first, implementation work equivalence second, evidence/observation density third, and broad contextual corroboration last. Raw observation counts are evidence density, never incident counts. Broad GitHub issue/PR anchors that are not strong case anchors are CONTEXT_ONLY and must not be described as the case or thread. Work-graph equivalence is implementation linkage, not incident identity. Under bootstrap byte pressure, duplicated older-window source/artifact detail yields before concrete 24h case examples, context-only anchors, and highlights.","state":"PROVEN","evidence":["github:organicoverlords/regression-research#627","github:organicoverlords/regression-research#628","git:organicoverlords/regression-research@a0d82eee76ddc9f7d1b8ea84aa0e0364efe093de","git:organicoverlords/regression-research@d9c4d727d312478ef3b931e08c9e9fd1e297c30a","task:Vault Timeline Materializer","worker-report:manual-20260906T0656-timeline-narrative-hierarchy"],"supersedes":[],"source_messages":["make sure bootstrap and timeline and vault are coherent user experience now and does not generate debugging or inconsistency problems like making your hierarchy have holes or make you stupid in debugging etc like before","go"],"interpretation":"The screenshot exposed a remaining narrative hierarchy leak: a broad umbrella issue anchor could be worded as if it corroborated one incident thread, and raw observation volume could dominate the answer. The stable correction is to encode case-first semantics and evidence priority directly in the timeline/bootstrap payload instead of relying on assistant inference.","confidence":100,"confidence_reason":"PR #627 and #628 required verification passed. Live 12.8k-event projection after #628 is 3796 bytes and preserves 19 24h cases including 1 RED case, 182 evidence-density observations, two concrete highlights, and regression-research#125 explicitly as CONTEXT_ONLY with 80 observations; work graph is explicitly implementation equivalence, not incident identity.","thread":"vault-timeline-materialized-ingestion","turn_task":"go","id":"mem-20260906-22852e77","timestamp":"2026-09-06T07:21:33+03:00"}
+{"kind":"lesson","scope":"tiny3d#20","tags":["improvement","proof","assistant-recorded","verbatim-source"],"title":"Generic flight contracts need explicit deterministic transitions","text":"Tiny3D generic flight-locomotion contracts previously persisted required actions without a deterministic required transition graph. PR #349 added canonical transitions, including takeoff only for flying_ground_creature, and regression-bound fly+glide to the existing non-avian winged transition contract.","state":"PROVEN","evidence":["tiny3d PR #349; merge a192a31919768752000c512f7d7ddb5e17382dcd; issue #20 comment https://github.com/organicoverlords/tiny3d/issues/20#issuecomment-5556902989"],"supersedes":[],"source_messages":["go"],"interpretation":"This is a reusable contract invariant: declaring flight action names is insufficient for #20; downstream authoring/proof needs a deterministic state-transition graph derived from canonical mode order and role capability, without inventing runtime success.","confidence":100,"confidence_reason":"Merged Tiny3D PR #349 on main; 827/827 local tests and hosted audit-tests/unit passed on the exact head.","project":"tiny3d","thread":"github:organicoverlords/tiny3d#20","turn_task":"go","id":"mem-20260906-18fb1279","timestamp":"2026-09-06T07:31:21+03:00"}
+{"kind":"lesson","scope":"tiny3d#127","tags":["improvement","proof","assistant-recorded","verbatim-source"],"title":"Humanoid P3 requests should reuse exact animation-quality identities","text":"Tiny3D #127 already had deterministic package and animation-quality identities but lacked one small package-bound P3 runtime request. PR #350 reused build_p3_animation_expectation to bind all 11 exact clip IDs and 17 quality-passed transitions, added the required gameplay sequences, and kept runtime/rendered acceptance pending.","state":"PROVEN","evidence":["tiny3d PR #350; merge 51371e42bf6655630a08df6f8b1f678a71ce4d80; issue #127 final comment"],"supersedes":[],"source_messages":["go"],"interpretation":"For authored animation sets, downstream runtime requests should bind the exact verified package and reuse the canonical animation-quality expectation instead of duplicating clip/transition identity logic or copying large payloads.","confidence":100,"confidence_reason":"Merged Tiny3D PR #350 as 51371e42; 833/833 local tests and hosted audit-tests/unit passed on exact head bfe8883.","project":"tiny3d","thread":"github:organicoverlords/tiny3d#127","turn_task":"go","id":"mem-20260906-674546b2","timestamp":"2026-09-06T07:42:57+03:00"}
+{"kind":"lesson","scope":"tiny3d#127","tags":["improvement","proof","assistant-recorded","verbatim-source"],"title":"Portable runtime request schemas must fail closed on nested identity shape","text":"Tiny3D PR #350 added an exact fail-closed #127 runtime request verifier, but its companion JSON Schema initially typed package and canonical nested policy subtrees only as generic objects/arrays. A schema-only P3 consumer could therefore accept malformed identity shape that Tiny3D verification would reject. The follow-up tree requires exact package identity fields/hash shapes, closes unknown package/expectation fields, fixes 11 clip/17 transition cardinalities, and schema-locks canonical gameplay/proof policy.","state":"PROVEN","evidence":["tiny3d PR #350 merge 51371e42bf6655630a08df6f8b1f678a71ce4d80; follow-up PR #351 head 75df27512ace75b993b1816be8b6f194d3a4e118; issue #127 comment https://github.com/organicoverlords/tiny3d/issues/127#issuecomment-5556973791"],"supersedes":[],"source_messages":["go"],"interpretation":"Portable request transport has two validation surfaces: semantic verification and JSON Schema. Exact semantic verification does not compensate for a permissive portable schema when downstream consumers may validate schema independently; both surfaces should fail closed on identity and canonical policy shape.","confidence":100,"confidence_reason":"The permissive schema was inspected directly; the hardened tree passed 833/833 repository tests, focused tests, real repaired-package request/schema replay, and has isolated PR #351.","project":"tiny3d","thread":"github:organicoverlords/tiny3d#127","turn_task":"go","id":"mem-20260906-f7097cd8","timestamp":"2026-09-06T07:45:20+03:00"}
+{"kind":"lesson","scope":"vault/timeline/materialized-ingestion","tags":["timeline","debugging","classification","legacy-compatibility","assistant-recorded","verbatim-source"],"title":"Legacy fallback applies only to genuinely unstructured history","text":"Structured modern records must never be relabeled as incidents/regressions from incidental title, scope, repository, or filename vocabulary. Legacy title/scope inference is compatibility only for genuinely unstructured historical records. Canonical assistant-recorded memories use structured categories/tags; workers with finding_tags use those tags; structured non-incident artifacts use provenance type. Old incident reports may still use title text to recover missing RED severity. Case provenance distinguishes MIXED from LEGACY_DEPENDENT so an old supporting observation does not weaken a case whose semantics are independently structured.","state":"PROVEN","evidence":["github:organicoverlords/regression-research#630","github:organicoverlords/regression-research#631","git:organicoverlords/regression-research@f6de660bf5c60bb1a52cae7a5fdd71ccdb2a778a","git:organicoverlords/regression-research@02dcdca9845fe5f98abfdd9cfc78cbcbd115c08b","task:Vault Timeline Materializer","worker-report:manual-20260906T0741-timeline-second-order-coherence"],"supersedes":[],"source_messages":["go","make sure bootstrap and timeline and vault are coherent user experience now and does not generate debugging or inconsistency problems like making your hierarchy have holes or make you stupid in debugging etc like before"],"interpretation":"A second-order audit found legacy compatibility inference still created false continuity cases from modern structured prose and names. The stable fix is source-aware fallback eligibility plus narrow phrase matching, while preserving genuine old title-only signal recovery.","confidence":100,"confidence_reason":"PR #630 and #631 required verification passed. Live 13,149-event incremental reclassification removed the known regression-coverage-matrix, Regression Research research-report, taxonomy-correction, and modern status false cases without source rebuild; 24h now has 10 cases with 1 RED, and exactly two 7d cases remain legacy-dependent, both old RED incident reports whose RED severity is title-only.","thread":"vault-timeline-materialized-ingestion","turn_task":"go","id":"mem-20260906-c7b49ba1","timestamp":"2026-09-06T08:02:39+03:00"}
+{"kind":"lesson","scope":"vault/timeline/materialized-ingestion","tags":["timeline","debugging","classification","authority-boundary","assistant-recorded","verbatim-source"],"title":"Memory semantic category is retrieval context, not continuity incident authority","text":"A Vault memory semantic_category may describe what a record is about for retrieval, but it must not by itself promote that memory into a continuity incident or the modern error lane. Continuity promotion comes from explicit signal tags, structured provenance/source signals, or the bounded compatibility path for genuinely unstructured old history. The forensic errors view may still retrieve old unstructured descriptive notes without turning that retrieval match into a case.","state":"PROVEN","evidence":["github:organicoverlords/regression-research#632","git:organicoverlords/regression-research@50ae153a7a1293ff3f6d102827cd4834c7465a41","task:Vault Timeline Materializer","worker-report:manual-20260906T0741-timeline-second-order-coherence"],"supersedes":[],"source_messages":["go","make sure bootstrap and timeline and vault are coherent user experience now and does not generate debugging or inconsistency problems like making your hierarchy have holes or make you stupid in debugging etc like before"],"interpretation":"A live self-test showed the memory retrieval classifier could label a lesson about incidents as semantic_category INCIDENT, and the timeline incorrectly treated that content taxonomy as case/error authority. PR #632 separates retrieval taxonomy, forensic recall, and continuity promotion.","confidence":100,"confidence_reason":"PR #632 required verify passed and merged. Live incremental materialization at 2026-09-06T15:38:50+03:00 reclassified 15,551 retained observations without a source rebuild: 24h is 7 cases with 1 RED; the taxonomy-only vault-timeline-materialized-ingestion and vault-memory-bootstrap-automatic-learning false cases are absent; mem-20260906-c7b49ba1 remains semantic_category INCIDENT but continuity MEMORY with no traits, no case, and no error-view match; an old unstructured slopwall note remains error-retrievable.","thread":"vault-timeline-materialized-ingestion","turn_task":"go","id":"mem-20260906-eadf99b8","timestamp":"2026-09-06T15:41:16+03:00"}
+{"kind":"lesson","scope":"chatgpt-mcp-clean#81 security reroute causality","tags":["route_problem","improvement","assistant-recorded","verbatim-source"],"title":"MCP tool safety annotations are a bounded mitigation, not proven reroute cause","text":"Fresh reroute reports persisted after exact d6e2972 production restore while public/local MCP health and immediate follow-up calls remained healthy. The process tools had no MCP safety annotations, so read_output was not explicitly advertised read-only/non-destructive. PR #132 merged accurate annotations at d65bff1 with focused clone-contract proof; production was intentionally left unchanged. Treat annotation impact on platform reroutes as unproven until real user-visible evidence after an explicitly authorized deployment.","state":"PROVISIONAL","evidence":["organicoverlords/chatgpt-mcp-clean#81; PR #132; merge d65bff15e4cdb97b6cb4f0ae836e1f2fda846fea; C:\\Users\\Lauri\\Desktop\\vault\\02 Evidence\\mcp-security-routing-events.jsonl; production backend-3011-17380-1788658484979"],"supersedes":[],"source_messages":["stillgettingsecurityreroutesourmcpstillneedsfixing"],"interpretation":"This preserves the narrowest reusable finding: a concrete MCP-controlled metadata gap was fixed off-path, but current evidence does not justify claiming the platform reroute was caused by MCP or deploying speculative runtime changes without the serving-path gate.","confidence":95,"confidence_reason":"Tool contract, source diff, isolated tools/list contract test, live edge/health checks, issue/PR state, and production generation were directly verified in this run; causal effect on platform routing was not measured.","project":"chatgpt-mcp-clean","thread":"thread:mcp-security-reroute-causality","turn_task":"stillgettingsecurityreroutesourmcpstillneedsfixing","id":"mem-20260906-4938efdc","timestamp":"2026-09-06T17:03:48+03:00"}
+{"kind":"lesson","scope":"vault/timeline/materialized-ingestion","tags":["timeline","debugging","graph","materialization","assistant-recorded","verbatim-source"],"title":"Snapshot case samples are not the continuity graph","text":"A timeline snapshot may expose only bounded continuity-case examples for orientation, but that sample must never masquerade as the complete case set. The periodic materializer should persist the full continuity graph once with member and signal-event IDs, while readers report matched, returned, and store case counts separately. Materialized readers must reuse the canonical forensic error selector and structural project/thread filters. If the deep event store reaches its cap, coverage becomes incomplete and no-match is not proof of absence.","state":"PROVEN","evidence":["github:organicoverlords/regression-research#634","github:organicoverlords/regression-research#125","git:organicoverlords/regression-research@f85fa068fd773b8027dc47c54ef37beeb45cc7dd","task:Vault Timeline Materializer","worker-report:manual-20260906T1645-timeline-case-graph-coherence"],"supersedes":[],"source_messages":["go","make sure bootstrap and timeline and vault are coherent user experience now and does not generate debugging or inconsistency problems like making your hierarchy have holes or make you stupid in debugging etc like before"],"interpretation":"The coherence audit found snapshot continuity_cases arrays silently contained only bounded examples despite larger summary counts, and the deep store lacked a complete queryable case graph. PR #634 makes examples explicit, persists the full graph, unifies materialized error semantics, tightens project scoping, and makes event-cap truncation absence-unsafe.","confidence":100,"confidence_reason":"PR #634 required verification passed and merged. Live incremental materialization at 17:04 EEST retained 16,135 observations without truncation and persisted 111 continuity cases in a ~124 KB graph. Snapshot metadata explicitly reports 7/7, 4/35, and 4/43 examples for 24h/3d/7d. A live mcp security reroute query resolves 1/111 cases with direct member and signal-event IDs; bootstrap overview remains 3,782 bytes and scheduled task Last Result is 0.","thread":"vault-timeline-materialized-ingestion","turn_task":"go","id":"mem-20260906-d6fc0b44","timestamp":"2026-09-06T17:09:05+03:00"}
+{"kind":"lesson","scope":"chatgpt-mcp-clean#81 production deployment","tags":["route_problem","contention","proof","assistant-recorded","verbatim-source"],"title":"MCP #81 deployment guard preserved foreign work and blocked pre-cutover","text":"Explicit deployment of PR #132 was attempted through the canonical guarded replacement path after PR #133 repaired the production server hash pin and isolated verifier receipt state. Final candidate 59b566f passed process-contract and WireGuard off-path proof, and the production gate passed. Transaction ded4be99-2e27-48ef-a24a-49e9c6eab687 ended FAILED_PRE_CUTOVER because old backend 3011 still had four direct child processes after the bounded drain window. Receipt proves runtime_changed=false and production_task_stopped=false; public/local production remained d6e2972/backend-3011-17380 and Caddy returned to its canonical hash. No foreign work was killed. Candidate 3012 remains isolated only because three foreign Tiny3D jobs were still live at rollback.","state":"PROVEN","evidence":["organicoverlords/chatgpt-mcp-clean#81; PR #132; PR #133; transaction ded4be99-2e27-48ef-a24a-49e9c6eab687; master 59b566f5106ff22ef2a700edb4012ba339cc756c; production d6e2972fd8da4247b164e2194366f84f2bdf8846"],"supersedes":[],"source_messages":["deploy PR #132 to the live MCP production serving path"],"interpretation":"This is a proven deployment-safety outcome, not a failed transport repair: the source mitigation is ready but not deployed. A future retry should use the same guarded path only after current live work naturally drains; do not kill foreign jobs or infer deployment from merged source.","confidence":100,"confidence_reason":"Direct immutable guardian receipt, live runtime HEAD/health, public health, VPS Caddy hash, candidate health, and Busy release were verified in this run.","project":"chatgpt-mcp-clean","thread":"thread:mcp-security-reroute-causality","turn_task":"deploy PR #132 to the live MCP production serving path","id":"mem-20