+{"kind":"lesson","scope":"mcp-security-reroute/client-tool-snapshot-and-deployment-acceptance","tags":["mcp","route_problem","proof","tooling","assistant-recorded","verbatim-source"],"title":"MCP annotations need client refresh and safe drain","text":"PRs #132/#133/#134 make the process-tool safety annotations real, pinned, and replacement-tested, but server deployment alone cannot establish client use or efficacy: the retained production transport window had 86 initialize responses and zero tools/list responses, consistent with ChatGPT using a frozen app/action tool snapshot. The first guarded deployment attempt failed safely before cutover because foreign child processes had not drained; production remained exact d6e2972. One drain blocker was an unnecessary Tiny3D recursive machine-root artifact scan; the exact artifact was already present in the canonical Tiny3D library index.","state":"PROVEN","evidence":["https://github.com/organicoverlords/chatgpt-mcp-clean/issues/81#issuecomment-5559844263","C:\\Users\\Lauri\\AppData\\Local\\ChatGPTMcpClean\\.state\\production-replacement\\receipt-ded4be99-2e27-48ef-a24a-49e9c6eab687.json","https://github.com/organicoverlords/chatgpt-mcp-clean/pull/134","C:\\Users\\Lauri\\Desktop\\Tiny3D_LIBRARY\\.tiny3d\\library\\index-v1.json"],"supersedes":[],"source_messages":["go"],"interpretation":"Treat annotation mitigation acceptance as a three-stage boundary: server emits/pins annotations, ChatGPT app/action definitions are refreshed or republished so the client can consume them, then real user-visible reroute behavior is observed. Preserve foreign work during deployment drain; do not weaken the guardian. Use canonical Tiny3D indexes instead of broad filesystem discovery.","confidence":99,"confidence_reason":"Supported by controlled MCP/OAuth tools/list A/B, the retained production transport log, merged PRs #132/#133/#134, the immutable FAILED_PRE_CUTOVER replacement receipt, and the canonical Tiny3D library index. Annotation effect on reroute rate itself remains explicitly unproven.","project":"chatgpt-mcp-clean","thread":"thread:mcp-security-reroute-causality","turn_task":"go","id":"mem-20260906-7f22cf73","timestamp":"2026-09-06T17:35:57+03:00"}
